claims:
1. A computer-implemented method for managing playback of pre-recorded digital conversations, the method executed between one or more servers and a user device, comprising the steps of:
receiving a pre-recorded digital conversation comprising a playback of a sequence of message segments;
sequentially presenting the sequence of message segments on the user device, the display of each subsequent message segment being separated by a time interval;
in response to a first user interaction type, cutting short a current time interval and advancing the playback of the displayed sequence to a subsequent message segment;
in response to a second user interaction type, pausing the playback; and
in response to a third user interaction type, resuming the paused playback and cutting short the current time interval and advancing the playback of the displayed sequence to a subsequent message segment.

9. The method of claim 1, further comprising:
receiving a set of user data for a first user, the user data including at least a set of reading or listening preferences;
for each message segment in the sequence, determining a comprehension time required for the first user to digest the content of the segment, the determination based on the received set of user data;
for each message segment in the sequence, classifying the segment based on the identity of the entity that sent the segment;
calculating, for each message segment in the sequence, a dwell time, the dwell time representing the length of time for which the segment is to be presented to the first user before presenting the next segment in the sequence, the dwell time being used as the time interval for sequentially presenting the message segments.
